From b47aed44033490ee0fbddfd8ce62f2d9ed4aea67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 0xFFshell <0xffshell@users.noreply.gitlab.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 06:48:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Close the unspelled writes in the counted edges and pin the
 comment stripper

A second read of 0034-0037, made against the game's own API (javap on the
official 26.3 jar) instead of the diffs. Every hole was proved first with a
mutation probe on the unmodified tip, and every new entry now fails the same
probe on its own line. No product file changes.

- KeyWritesTest: WRITES gains makeJump(, resetToggleKeys( and
  restoreToggleStatesOnScreenClosed( - 0037 called resetToggleKeys
  configuration, but it is a bulk setDown(false) on the toggle mappings and
  its twin a bulk setDown(true) - and consumeClick(. The census reads
  getMoveVector( and hasForwardImpulse( as well as input.keyPresses.
- ButtonWritesTest: BUTTONS gains .gameMode, the controller itself, which
  covers every public MultiPlayerGameMode hand method (handleContainerInput,
  interact, releaseUsingItem, dropItem, handlePickItem*, ...) instead of eight
  more spellings. The "only place mc.gameMode is touched" comment is
  corrected: BlockBreakHelper names it to clear its destroy delay.
- HandWritesTest: pickSlot( and addAndPickItem(, vanilla's pick path to a
  selected slot.
- ClickGatesTest#stripComments is literal-aware (a // or /* inside a string,
  a character or a text block is not a comment) and a stripped comment leaves
  its line break or a space, so neighbours are never joined. StripCommentsTest
  pins nine cases, seven of which fail against the old helper.
- HUMANLIKE.md: the two sentences that list these guards.

Suite: 43 classes / 356 tests / 0 failures (347 + 9 new).
